.TH GIT-DIFF-HTML 1 "October 2026" "git-diff-html 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-diff-html \- generate a side-by-side HTML report of Git differences
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-diff-html
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIref\fR] [\fIfile ...\fR]
.br
.B git-diff-html
.BR \-r " \fIREF1 REF2\fR [" \fIfile ...\fR ]
.br
.B git-diff-html
.BI FILE_OLD " " FILE_NEW
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-diff-html
renders the differences in a Git repository as a Gerrit/BeyondCompare-style
side-by-side HTML report with inline highlighting.  The report is a single
self-contained HTML file that can be opened in any modern browser.
Outside a Git repository, two files can be compared directly with
.BR "git-diff-html FILE_OLD FILE_NEW" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the report to \fIFILE\fR (default: a temporary file under ~/git-diff-html/).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-commit " \fIREF\fR"
Compare against \fIREF\fR (default: \fIHEAD\fR).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-range " \fIREF1 REF2\fR"
Compare two commits directly.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-staged
Show staged changes (equivalent to \fBgit diff \-\-cached\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-no-open
Do not open the report in a browser after generation.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-syntax
Disable C/C++ syntax highlighting on context lines.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-context " \fIN\fR"
Number of context lines around changes (default: 3).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git-diff-html
Working tree versus HEAD, and open the report.
.TP
.B git-diff-html abc123
Working tree versus commit abc123.
.TP
.B git-diff-html -r aaa bbb
Commit aaa versus commit bbb.
.TP
.B git-diff-html old.c new.c
Compare two files side by side, outside a Git repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-diff (1)
